{title: Amazing Grace}
{artist: John Newton (words), traditional (melody)}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 80}
{meta: public_domain Words by John Newton, published 1779 in Olney Hymns. Melody "New Britain", published 1829.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[G]mazing [G]grace, how [G7]sweet the [C]sound
That [G]saved a [G]wretch like [D]me![D]
I [G]once was [G]lost, but [G7]now am [C]found,
Was [G]blind, but [D]now I [G]see.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
'Twas [G]grace that [G]taught my [G7]heart to [C]fear,
And [G]grace my [G]fears re[D]lieved;[D]
How [G]precious [G]did that [G7]grace ap[C]pear
The [G]hour I [D]first be[G]lieved.[G]
{end_of_verse}
